  "critique": {
    "axis": "aesthetics",
    "evidence": "Strong cyber-editorial art direction, disciplined cyan/green/red semantics, crisp cards, and thoughtful desktop-to-mobile restructuring. However, desktop hierarchy is imbalanced: the oversized headline dominates while the explanatory callout floats in empty space and the visualization feels underscaled. Tablet is the most resolved. Mobile remains polished but dense, with very small diagram and metadata text; the header’s truncated navigation and low-contrast labels look cramped rather than fully intentional.",
    "fix": "Rebalance the desktop hero into a tighter grid, enlarge the meaningful visualization, and reduce dead space. On mobile, increase diagram/metadata legibility and give the horizontally scrolling header a clearer, higher-contrast active state and edge treatment.",
